{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_10-41-34-etcd_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v3.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 3,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A caller proposes through RawNode or Node.run. Followers may forward; leaders reject proposals during transfer/removal or quota exhaustion. Accepted entries get leader term and consecutive index, enter unstable log and generate deferred self append support. Replication carries preceding index/term, entries and commit. Followers match the preceding entry, refuse committed conflicts, append only the conflicting suffix and acknowledge through the resulting prefix; stale prefixes can acknowledge the existing committed boundary. Ready or asynchronous local append envelopes impose the storage-before-response contract. Successful current-term tracked replies update per-peer Match. The active voter majority order statistic, minimum across both joint halves, supplies a candidate commit index; raftLog advances only when its entry term matches current leader term. Append broadcasts and bounded heartbeat commit propagate the decision. Ready then supplies committed entries, with asynchronous application restricted to locally stable entries and snapshots blocking entry application. Advance or apply response reports completion; the caller owns actual state-machine effects and client acknowledgement. Propose success alone is not commitment.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-entry\",\n        \"B-propose\",\n        \"B-follower-append\",\n        \"B-storage-release\",\n        \"B-aggregate\",\n        \"B-apply\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-app-queued\",\n        \"F-match\",\n        \"F-committed\",\n        \"F-apply-reported\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"entry\",\n        \"leader-admit\",\n        \"candidate-follower\",\n        \"send-replication\",\n        \"append-receive\",\n        \"log-start-append\",\n        \"reply-queue\",\n        \"async-contract\",\n        \"leader-match\",\n        \"tracker-commit\",\n        \"majority\",\n        \"joint\",\n        \"log-eligibility\",\n        \"log-apply\",\n        \"ready-contract\",\n        \"node-loop\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Election ticks or Campaign pass eligibility and unapplied-configuration guards. PreVote collects support without changing term/vote; real campaign increments term and records self vote, counted only after deferred response release. Incoming votes require voting eligibility and last term/index freshness. The candidate accepts its phase-specific response type, records first vote per identity and uses active joint voter quorums; winning installs leadership and an empty entry. Higher term normally resets role, votes, remote progress and readOnly acknowledgements, with pre-vote and check-quorum lease exceptions. Lower-term replies do not reach ordinary consumers. Same-term leader traffic demotes candidates. Optional CheckQuorum revokes local leadership on inactive quorum; transfer catches up a voter then sends TimeoutNow, rejects new proposals while pending and aborts on timeout. Application activates membership; learner promotion/removal and joint exit change future quorum interpretation. Restart loads term/vote/commit and membership from Storage then becomes follower. Snapshot restore preserves committed prefix constraints, replaces history/config if needed and prevents campaigning while installation is pending.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-campaign\",\n        \"B-election-result\",\n        \"B-context\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-vote-queued\",\n        \"F-leader\",\n        \"F-config\",\n        \"F-committed\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"campaign\",\n        \"step-vote\",\n        \"roles\",\n        \"term-filter\",\n        \"ticks\",\n        \"candidate-follower\",\n        \"leader-other\",\n        \"tracker-votes\",\n        \"majority\",\n        \"joint\",\n        \"config-change\",\n        \"config-activate\",\n        \"startup\",\n        \"snapshot-restore\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Formation support is scoped by current role/term and interpreted by application-activated membership. Reset discards remote Match and prior vote/read acknowledgements but does not erase log or committed prefix; election freshness and current-term commit gating reconnect inherited history to new decisions. Configuration changes preserve existing peer Match, initialize new peers at zero, and recompute commitment under new voters; staged learners remain outgoing voters until joint exit. Queued storage completions keep their originating raft term: stale entry append completion cannot trim unstable entries, while committed snapshot/application completion remains meaningful across terms. Pending pre-current-term ReadIndex requests survive reset separately from the cleared heartbeat acknowledgement tracker; a subsequent current-term commit reprocesses them through current read mode/quorum. Ready read results still require caller correlation and application progress. Storage, configuration and application boundaries therefore directly govern A1 support and A2 eligibility, without treating mere message emission or applied bookkeeping as durable or client completion. The synchronous Node API permits early Advance before command application finishes; its reported applied boundary can therefore precede completion of embedding work. The campaign scan reads that reported boundary. Asynchronous apply responses instead follow completed work under their separate contract. Configuration proposal admission also compares pendingConfIndex to reported applied, while joint-state checks and quorum aggregation consume installed membership. Configuration-triggered commitment lacks the pending-read release call present in the append-response path; public ReadIndex separately permits loss and retries.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-context\",\n        \"B-storage-release\",\n        \"B-membership\",\n        \"B-aggregate\",\n        \"B-read\",\n        \"B-apply\",\n        \"B-recovery\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"F-match\",\n        \"F-committed\",\n        \"F-config\",\n        \"F-read-index\",\n        \"F-apply-reported\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"reset-append\",\n        \"log-eligibility\",\n        \"config-change\",\n        \"config-activate\",\n        \"term-filter\",\n        \"storage-envelope\",\n        \"storage-tail\",\n        \"unstable-stable\",\n        \"apply-progress\",\n        \"read-pending\",\n        \"read-tracking\",\n        \"ready-contract\",\n        \"node-early-advance\",\n        \"doc-early-advance\",\n        \"advance\",\n        \"step-vote\",\n        \"campaign\",\n        \"conf-proposal-contract\",\n        \"mode-contract\",\n        \"membership-doc\",\n        \"read-api-contract\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Exact storage failure recovery for a production backend lies beyond the library snapshot; MemoryStorage is not a durable backend.\",\n      \"Progress flow-control variants and malformed input behavior require separate bounded questions.\",\n      \"The safety effect of consecutive configuration admissions when early Advance precedes activation needs a distinct same-group history; per-change validation and documented best-effort checks do not resolve it alone.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Both core lines have been followed through actual dispatch, producers, quorum consumers, context changes, configuration activation and caller handoffs. Usable is a bounded source explanation, not safety proof or execution evidence.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"66d036cf42454ab7b83ed497e1039f0e\",\n      \"version\": 1,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"66d036cf42454ab7b83ed497e1039f0e\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"d26b6eac66bb4e99a29ba0883a623b58\",\n      \"version\": 2,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"d26b6eac66bb4e99a29ba0883a623b58\"\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"operation_id\": \"aea146a71f2a4332b50a611e8749b030\",\n      \"version\": 3,\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"aea146a71f2a4332b50a611e8749b030\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"next_objective\": {\n    \"action\": \"investigate_and_refocus\",\n    \"boundary\": \"both_core_paths\",\n    \"reason\": \"Use results to update understanding and compare the remaining frontier\",\n    \"core_gaps\": []\n  },\n  \"drafts\": [],\n  \"candidates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ad63501da0fe49099ab4a465808db9e9\",\n      \"status\": \"paused\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stage\": \"analyze\",\n      \"read_plan_id\": null,\n      \"stagnation\": 0,\n      \"obligation_id\": \"C-storage-qualified-commit\",\n      \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n      \"current_applicability\": \"within_recorded_scope\",\n      \"executions\": [\n        {\n          \"check_id\": \"1cbbcd58eb824f779c088d377fd008d3\",\n          \"artifact_id\": \"d5859ae3d2754082b6f2257a1ed629d2\",\n          \"action\": \"direct_check\",\n          \"status\": \"completed\",\n          \"outcome\": \"tests_passed\",\n          \"record\": {\n            \"path\": \"state.json\",\n            \"collection\": \"checks\",\n            \"match\": {\n              \"id\": \"1cbbcd58eb824f779c088d377fd008d3\"\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      ],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"question_candidates\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"id\": \"ad63501da0fe49099ab4a465808db9e9\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"result_claim_ids\": [\n        \"C-storage-qualified-commit\"\n      ],\n      \"question_preview\": \"Can leader commitment of a current-term proposal advance before the replicas whose storage workers have completed matching appends constitute the active voting majority, when the leader append worker is finitely delayed?\",\n      \"audit_spec_version\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0f9e8d1e51f64b34a017f21c8f359d94\",\n      \"question\": {\n        \"audit_spec_version\": 2,\n        \"disposition\": \"ready_for_check\",\n        \"preferred_check\": \"controlled_schedule\",\n        \"requests\": [],\n        \"question\": \"Does the pending-read consumer release a request waiting for the first current-term commit when that commit is established by application-activated membership, under the synchronous Node early-Advance contract?\",\n        \"importance\": \"A retained request can depend on an unrelated future proposal despite the commit precondition being satisfied. This is an implementation progress-contract question; it does not itself imply unsafe reads or a public guarantee that ReadIndex never drops requests.\",\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"advance\",\n          \"append-receive\",\n          \"apply-accept\",\n          \"apply-progress\",\n          \"async-contract\",\n          \"bootstrap\",\n          \"campaign\",\n          \"campaign-config-test\",\n          \"candidate-follower\",\n          \"conf-contract\",\n          \"config-activate\",\n          \"config-change\",\n          \"config-restore\",\n          \"doc-early-advance\",\n          \"entry\",\n          \"joint\",\n          \"leader-admit\",\n          \"leader-match\",\n          \"leader-other\",\n          \"log-apply\",\n          \"log-commit-apply\",\n          \"log-eligibility\",\n          \"majority\",\n          \"mode-contract\",\n          \"node-control-methods\",\n          \"node-early-advance\",\n          \"node-loop\",\n          \"pending-read-intent\",\n          \"progress-update\",\n          \"read-api-contract\",\n          \"read-pending\",\n          \"read-release\",\n          \"read-tracking\",\n          \"ready-contract\",\n          \"ready-release\",\n          \"reply-queue\",\n          \"reset-append\",\n          \"roles\",\n          \"snapshot-restore\",\n          \"startup\",\n          \"step-vote\",\n          \"storage-envelope\",\n          \"storage-tail\",\n          \"term-filter\",\n          \"ticks\",\n          \"tracker-commit\",\n          \"tracker-votes\",\n          \"unstable-stable\"\n        ],\n        \"participants\": [\n          \"Synchronous Node leader\",\n          \"Application applying a delayed committed configuration\",\n          \"Voting peers\"\n        ],\n        \"objects\": [\n          \"Committed prefix\",\n          \"Unique pending ReadIndex request\",\n          \"Application-activated voter set\"\n        ],\n        \"contexts\": [\n          \"Synchronous early Advance before configuration activation, preserving Ready application order\",\n          \"Same leader term across the selected request and commit transition\",\n          \"ReadOnlySafe\"\n        ],\n        \"event_paths\": [\n          \"Node.ReadIndex -> stepLeader pendingReadIndexMessages -> Node.ApplyConfChange -> switchToConfig -> maybeCommit -> inspect pending queue after Stop barrier\",\n          \"Control: actual MsgAppResp first advances commit and invokes releasePendingReadIndexMessages\"\n        ],\n        \"activity_classes\": [\n          \"A1\",\n          \"A2\"\n        ],\n        \"behavior_ids\": [\n          \"B-read\",\n          \"B-aggregate\"\n        ],\n        \"fact_ids\": [\n          \"F-committed\"\n        ],\n        \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n          \"B-entry\": \"Documents and implements early Advance and serialized Node ownership.\",\n          \"B-campaign\": \"Election guard reads reported applied; early Advance makes its boundary relevant.\",\n          \"B-membership\": \"Application activates a changed majority and invokes commitment recomputation.\",\n          \"B-election-result\": \"Actual vote messages establish the new leader.\",\n          \"B-apply\": \"Advance reports application progress before deferred work finishes under the synchronous permission.\",\n          \"B-storage-release\": \"Persistence precedes release of all synchronous Ready messages in the driver.\"\n        },\n        \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n        \"counterevidence\": [\n          \"Public ReadIndex may be lost without notice and callers must retry; no unconditional external completion guarantee is asserted.\",\n          \"hasUnappliedConfChanges blocks a campaign with committed configuration changes above reported applied; the driver uses the documented early-Advance permission rather than assigning applied directly.\",\n          \"Ordinary append-response commitment invokes releasePendingReadIndexMessages.\",\n          \"Source exploration showed later read processing and an additional proposal can release the original request; this is not evidence of permanent loss.\"\n        ],\n        \"unknowns\": [\n          \"Whether affected deployments rely on this scheduling permission and whether any broader consequence follows are outside the local queue-release requirement.\"\n        ],\n        \"priority\": 1,\n        \"trigger_rationale\": \"Exploration 680ffdc882db43e0931033ebfd08b3de established the actual public-Node prefix and commitment transition, but is not property evidence. A stopped-owner observation can directly measure queue membership at this local endpoint, avoiding timeout-based liveness claims and concurrent private-state access.\"\n      },\n      \"status\": \"escalated\",\n      \"parent_candidate_id\": null,\n      \"fork_reason\": \"\",\n      \"stage\": \"analyze\",\n      \"read_plan_id\": null,\n      \"material_ids\": [],\n      \"spec_task_ids\": [],\n      \"stagnation\": 0,\n      \"stop_reason\": \"An explicit internal queue-processing expectation supplies a narrow implementation-semantic responsibility distinct from public read retry semantics.\",\n      \"resume_conditions\": [],\n      \"obligation_id\": \"C-first-commit-read-release\",\n      \"open_issue_ids\": [],\n      \"current_applicability\": \"within_recorded_scope\",\n      \"executions\": [\n        {\n          \"check_id\": \"d667238925ff4b54ac43bb5ae6f2a4f4\",\n          \"artifact_