"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"0f996326dd084144b630da3de531555d\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"feedback\": {\n        \"ref_ids\": [\n          \"leader-admit\",\n          \"conf-proposal-contract\",\n          \"mode-contract\",\n          \"node-early-advance\",\n          \"doc-early-advance\",\n          \"membership-doc\",\n          \"candidate-follower\"\n        ],\n        \"answered\": \"The proposed history keeps both compared leaders in the final voter set: start voters 1..5, defer application at leader 1 while persisting and advancing, propose removals of 2 then 3, and let other nodes activate final voters {1,4,5}. Partition {1,2,3} from {4,5}; all delivered messages come from actual Nodes. Nodes 2/3 remain running but are never re-added or assigned new state. The old side proposes a command; node 4 then campaigns through the public API. Independent stores and public commit indexes are the endpoint observations. Deferred application is subsequently completed in order without healing the partition.\",\n        \"remaining\": [\n          \"Execution must determine whether proposal validation, removed-peer handling, vote freshness or current-term commitment blocks the history.\",\n          \"Any differing entries require a later formal obligation and correspondence review, including the synchronous caller permission and continued operation of removed peers.\"\n        ],\n        \"understanding\": null,\n        \"rationale\": \"This construction tests two still-current members, avoids treating an obsolete removed leader as the sole endpoint, and uses actual producer messages. It can expose or refute disjoint support formation while preserving the source-documented caller and network boundaries.\",\n        \"question_updates\": {}\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pending_work\": [],\n  \"current\": {\n    \"phase\": \"executed\",\n    \"operation_id\": \"0f996326dd084144b630da3de531555d\",\n    \"action\