{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_agreement_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nclaim='C-configuration-commit-agreement'; binding='D-commit-agreement'\ng=dict(source_ids=['membership-doc','replicated-machine-expectation','log-start-append','leader-match','config-activate','node-early-advance','doc-early-advance'],expectation_ids=['replicated-machine-expectation','membership-doc'],binding_ids=[binding],derivation='The package promises a replicated log keeping replicated state machines in sync, and states that its application-activated one-node membership changes preserve safety through configuration overlap. The necessary log-agreement responsibility is that entries declared committed at the same log index on two participating nodes agree in term, type and command data. This is a necessity, not a requirement that every accepted proposal commit. The committed-conflict panic in maybeAppend is supporting code evidence, not the normative source. A default propose-time best-effort validator is not itself a safety guarantee.',applicability='Synchronous public Node with default configuration validation; successful storage and no crashes; sequential single-voter removals and a network partition. Both compared nodes remain members of the final activated configuration. Application may trail Advance under explicit documentation but must eventually apply all committed batches in order.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['ProposeConfChange can drop proposals, so actual committed entries and resulting configurations must be observed.','Best-effort validation can accept a configuration that later panics; this history must complete all required ApplyConfChange calls to distinguish that case.','A node with an uncommitted competing entry does not violate agreement; the antecedent requires both observed commit indexes to cover the selected index.'])\nq=dict(question='Can documented early Advance across sequential configuration changes permit two continuing members to commit different entries at one log index under their respective activated configurations?',importance='Different committed commands at the same replicated-log position can make state machines diverge. This check targets the consensus decision itself, not a dropped proposal or a timeout.',source_ids=['membership-doc','replicated-machine-expectation','node-early-advance','doc-early-advance','conf-proposal-contract','mode-contract'],participants=['Synchronous Node leaders and followers','Embedding application','Partitioned network'],objects=['Committed entry at a shared log index','Activated voter configuration','Reported applied boundary'],contexts=['Sequential simple voter removals with default validation','Early Advance while ordered application is finitely deferred','Two compared nodes retained in final membership'],event_paths=['Node.ProposeConfChange -> stepLeader admission -> actual replication and commitment -> early Advance versus ApplyConfChange','Old leader replication under old voter set; new leader Campaign and no-op replication under activated voter set -> stored entries and public commit indexes'],activity_classes=['A1','A2'],behavior_ids=['B-aggregate','B-follower-append'],fact_ids=['F-committed'],supporting_behavior_ids={'B-entry':'Synchronous caller permission and serialized ownership.','B-propose':'Configuration admission uses reported application progress.','B-apply':'Early Advance and actual ordered application can have different completion boundaries.','B-membership':'Actual configuration activation determines eligible support.','B-campaign':'Eligibility and freshness checks constrain acquisition of new authority.','B-election-result':'Actual votes establish leadership and append the new-term empty entry.','B-storage-release':'Actual Ready persistence precedes all emitted protocol support.'},obligation_relation_kind='preservation',counterevidence=['Node requires ordered completion of application batches; all deferred batches must finish in FIFO order.','Configuration validation is explicitly best-effort even when enabled; admission alone is not a defect witness.','Current-term commitment, vote freshness and configuration quorum checks remain enabled.','Removed nodes are kept running and only receive actual messages; their continued behavior is an applicability premise requiring correspondence review.'],unknowns=['Will the fixed formal history observe distinct entries covered by both commit indexes after all delayed configuration application finishes?','Does the fixed history comply with the documented synchronous application and membership duties, including continued removed-peer operation?'],priority=0,trigger_rationale='Exploration 1402378b0c5443a7b2c22a8f40fe41de reached different entries at index 9 on nodes 1 and 4, both final voters, and completed deferred application. This guides a formal check with an index selected before competing entries exist and a prompt-application control. Exploration is not property Evidence.',disposition='ready_for_check',preferred_check='controlled_schedule')\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v3.json'));refs=set(q['source_ids'])\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id'] in q['behavior_ids'] or b['id'] in q['supporting_behavior_ids']:refs.update(b['source_ids'])\nfor f in m['facts']:\n if f['id'] in q['fact_ids']:refs.update(f['source_ids'])\nq['source_ids']=sorted(refs)\nob=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='consensus_safety',description='For two participating nodes of the same replicated group, if both declare a log index committed, the entries at that index must agree in term, entry type and command data, including across application-activated membership changes.',source_ids=g['source_ids'],scope=dict(description='No-crash synchronous Node histories with default validation, sequential simple voter removals, ordered finite deferred application and partitioned actual network traffic; compared nodes remain members of final membership.',assumptions=['MemoryStorage models successful persistence without crash recovery.','All delivered network messages are produced by actual Nodes; no Byzantine state or identity reuse.','Removed peers continue processing actual messages without rejoining.','Application follows Ready order and calls ApplyConfChange for all committed configuration entries; synchronous early Advance is used.'],excluded=['Physical storage failures or recovery','Byzantine faults','Asynchronous storage','Client acknowledgement or application-output equality','Unconditional proposal progress under partition'],parameters={'async_storage_writes':False,'disable_conf_change_validation':False,'membership_changes':'sequential simple single-voter removals','application':'early Advance with finite FIFO delay versus prompt activation'}),pending=[],grounding=g)\nb=dict(id=binding,material_id='log-start-append',symbol='maybeAppend',start_line=105,end_line=129,description='Follower append enforces preservation of its already committed prefix while incorporating leader entries; agreement is independently observed through stores and public commit indexes.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=['replicated-machine-expectation','membership-doc','log-start-append','leader-match'],rationale='The shared committed-log responsibility constrains decisions across configurations; this follower guard is a protection, not a substitute for comparing separately formed decisions.')])\nleg=dict(source_ids=['node-start-and-restart','node-step-and-read','node-control-methods','node-loop','doc-early-advance','node-early-advance','bootstrap-contract','storage-memory','storage-snap-append','campaign','candidate-follower','config-activate','leader-admit','mode-contract','membership-doc','status-copy'],expectation_ids=['doc-early-advance','node-early-advance','conf-contract','conf-proposal-contract','membership-doc'],binding_ids=[binding],derivation='Five public Nodes start with identical bootstrap voters. Ready Entries and HardState are persisted before emitted messages or Advance; there are no snapshots, crashes or private state assignments. A real election establishes node 1. Propose removal of node 2 and drain actual traffic; then propose removal of node 3 and drain. In the delayed variant only node 1 defers every application batch in FIFO order while advancing after persistence under the explicit synchronous permission. Other peers apply all configurations normally. Removed peers remain alive and process only actual messages; no identity is reused. Partition {1,2,3} from {4,5} by retaining all actual cross-partition messages. Select the next log index from storage before either competing entry exists. Propose a normal command at node 1, then campaign node 4 with actual vote and replication messages. Finish every deferred node-1 application batch in original order and drain without healing the partition. Read both independent stores and public Status commit indexes. The prompt-application variant runs the same schedule but activates all configurations before advancing. It may leave the old-side command uncommitted, which is permitted. Stop all Nodes independently of equality.',applicability='No ticks or failure-detection deadline is assumed. Five-millisecond Ready waits and the bounded drain loop are scheduling controls, not the property oracle; timeout, missing entries or panic are incomplete execution. The two subtests are independent histories and never combined into one witness. Comparison uses a preselected index and scenario identity, not the differing entry terms or values.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['A stronger caller rule requiring configuration activation before Advance would exclude this history, but the acquired Node and doc.go statements explicitly permit Advance before application completion; correspondence must preserve that premise and any conflicting contract.','A committed conflict panic after healing is not needed or induced; independent committed endpoints are compared while the partition remains.'])\nplan=dict(description='Compare actual committed entries in two independent five-node histories with delayed versus prompt configuration activation, preserving all protocol guards and completing deferred application.',claim_id=claim,binding_ids=[binding],harness=dict(kind='go_test',source='',files={},description='Public Node network and MemoryStorage, two ordered removals, deterministic partition, actual old-side proposal and new-side campaign, ordered application completion and independent store observations.',semantic_changes=['No target modifications or private critical-state assignments.','Normal-entry application is a no-op; configuration entries call the actual ApplyConfChange.','MemoryStorage represents successful persistence under a no-crash assumption.','both_committed compares each public commit index against the independently preselected target index; entries_equal compares actual stored term/type/data. Raw operands are emitted.'],prerequisites=[dict(alias='comparison',event='comparison_admitted',conditions=[dict(field='history_ready',value=True)])],legality=leg),monitors=[dict(id='M-configuration-agreement',checker_id='configuration-agreement',event='agreement_observed',binding_ids=[binding],grounding=g,admission_alias='comparison',applicability_conditions=[])],observable_properties=[dict(checker_id='configuration-agreement',kind='event_implication',trigger=dict(field='completed',value=True),antecedent=dict(field='both_committed',value=True),assertion=dict(field='entries_equal',value=True),identity_fields=['scenario_id','target_index'],description='If both same-group nodes declare the independently selected index committed, their stored entries there must agree. A different uncommitted entry is permitted.')],uncertainties=['Applicability depends on the documented synchronous early-Advance permission covering delayed configuration application and continued processing by removed peers.','This bounded history does not establish all configuration schedules or an external client-visible application result.'])\njson.dump(plan,open('config-agreement-plan.json','w'),indent=2)\ns=dict(action='check',rationale='Test a concrete consensus agreement responsibility after exploration reached disjoint committed decisions; use actual producers, independent identity and a permitted noncommitting control.',candidate=dict(action='obligation',rationale='The replicated-log synchronization and safe membership-overlap statements ground committed-entry agreement across these actual contexts.',question=q,obligation=ob,bindings=[b]),plan_path='config-agreement-plan.json',harness_path='config_agreement_check_test.go',files={},sources=[],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['1402378b0c5443a7b2c22a8f40fe41de','membership-doc','node-early-advance','doc-early-advance','mode-contract'],answered='Exploration produced committed index 9 containing a term-2 command at node 1 and a term-3 empty entry at node 4. Both nodes remain final voters, and deferred configuration application subsequently completed. These are exploratory observations, not formal property Evidence. The fixed check selects its index before the competing entries, completes delayed application before observation, and adds a prompt-activation control.',remaining=['Execute the fixed formal check and review whole-check correspondence, especially early Advance, removed-peer behavior, actual configuration entries, and the committed-entry oracle.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='The formal comparison can distinguish a permitted uncommitted conflicting entry from two independently committed entries without assuming client completion or requiring partition healing.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_agreement_check.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_10-41-34-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
